mlx5e: xsk: pass desc.options to xsk_buff_get_metadata()

Debian linux 6.12.116+deb13-amd64 backports the upstream change that adds a third
"u32 options" argument to xsk_buff_get_metadata(); metadata is only
returned when XDP_TX_METADATA is set in the descriptor options.
The MLNX_OFED compat layer has no check for this and still uses the
two argument form, failing with:

  en/xsk/tx.c:122: error: too few arguments to function xsk_buff_get_metadata

Kernel specific: apply only when building for 6.12.116+deb13-amd64.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c	2026-11-12 19:26:10.253013363 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c	2026-11-12 19:26:10.429025626 +0000
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 #endif
 		xdptxd.len = desc.len;
 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_TX_METADATA_OPS
-		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr);
+		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr, desc.options);
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_BUFF_ALLOC
